Falsifies `interfaces_note::interface_verification::decode_interfaces_never_panics`.

The defect: `decode_interfaces` reads the version word with a plain `d[..4]`
instead of `d.get(..4).ok_or(Error::NoVersion)?`, the unchecked index a refactor
for brevity produces. A note shorter than four bytes then panics inside a loader
that is handed bytes from an untrusted binary rather than returning `NoVersion`.

Expected to fail: an index-out-of-bounds check inside `decode_interfaces`, on any
slice shorter than four bytes.


diff --git a/crates/interfaces_note/src/lib.rs b/crates/interfaces_note/src/lib.rs
index 70afb0cb6..6ee7b05d0 100644
--- a/crates/interfaces_note/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/interfaces_note/src/lib.rs
@@ -203,7 +203,7 @@ fn record(r: &[u8]) -> Declared {
 ///
 /// Name: provisional, minted 2026-10-31 (UTC) by lane milestone/956-checkable-interface-versions.
 pub fn decode_interfaces(d: &[u8]) -> Result<Interfaces<'_>, Error> {
-    let version = d.get(..4).ok_or(Error::NoVersion)?;
+    let version = &d[..4];
     if u32::from_le_bytes([version[0], version[1], version[2], version[3]]) != INTERFACES_VERSION {
         return Err(Error::UnknownVersion);
     }
